  "query_preview": "(This evening through Saturday)...\nIssued at 244 PM EDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nWidely scattered showers and storms will continue across portions of \ncentral Indiana this afternoon, though modest instability and weak \nshear is limiting coverage and intensity significantly. This \nactivity should largely come to an end this evening as heating is \nlost, though a weak upper wave may allow a few showers to linger, \nmainly north.\n\nA slightly more substantial upper wave arrives Sunday, and will \npromote scattered to potentially widespread showers and storms, \nparticularly during the afternoon and evening hours. Modest \ninstability and deep layer shear may promote slightly better \ncoverage and a slight uptick in intensity tomorrow, and possibly a \nsmall hail threat in addition to the localized strong wind threat, \nand the continued heavy downpour threat.\n\nThough the surface front pushes further south as we move into the \nwork week, a slow-moving upper level low will pass through the area \nthrough mid week, with chances for showers and perhaps a few \nthunderstorms lingering into Wednesday, though chances should be \nhighest when diurnally favored/near peak heating.\n\nHigh pressure in the wake of the upper low should bring mild and \npleasant weather to the area late in the week.\n\nTemperatures will remain warm through Sunday, though the gradient \nwill be relatively strong with the surface front in the area. Once \nthe front is shuttled southward, temperatures through the remainder \nof the period should be near to below normal, with highs largely in \nthe 70s and lows largely in the 50s from Monday onward.",
